Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:50:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: add NXP/Goodix TFA987X (TFA9872/9873/9874)
 amplifier driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add an ASoC codec driver for the TFA9872/9873/9874 smart amplifiers used
as speaker amps on boards such as the OnePlus 8 Pro (two TFA9874 on
i2c15, binding nxp,tfa987x from the previous commit).

The driver programs the amplifier directly over I2C via regmap with
readable/writeable/volatile register ranges. It acquires the VDDD supply
and the active-high reset GPIO, validates the chip revision against the
compatible, and writes every managed register as a full 16-bit value to
a safe default after the I2C soft reset: powered down, amplifier off,
boost converter off at reset defaults, 16-bit single-slot TDM input on
the slot selected by sound-channel.

The amplifier starts muted with minimum gain. Hardware enable requires
all three of DAPM power, the user "Playback Switch" and an unmuted
playback stream; the transitions are serialized under a mutex and a
control-bus error is latched off with the amplifier held in reset,
requiring rebind. A raw "Playback Volume" gain control is exposed
without any unverified dB conversion. Component suspend powers the
amplifier down and resume restores the register defaults while keeping
the user gain; unbind silences the amplifier before reset and VDDD are
removed.

Register field definitions follow the public GPL-2.0-only community
driver tfa987x.c (gitlab.nura.eco soc/qualcomm-sm8250/linux @
3c5440e9dd3c), which credits the NXP tfa98xx register definitions
(Copyright 2014-2020 NXP Semiconductors). No vendor firmware,
calibration data or decompiled code is used.

Signed-off-by: Mikkel Inumineq Jørgensen <6770514+inumineq@users.noreply.github.com>
